From 52df4256be3e1c1fcb7262e89cce1826ac244fc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:13:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] T4890: a recall next to a reply's own question goes out as
 its own message
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The founder's thread 51037 (13 Oct, 09:00Z): a reply about one contact's
Kazakhstan reach asked the owner its own question, and 2608's recall of
another contact's need was added under it with its two buttons. The message
held two questions, and „კი, დააკავშირე" answered the recall instead of the
reply. When the reply already asks something and does not speak of the person
in need, the recall now goes out as its own message right after it, with the
same line and the same two buttons. The reply keeps its question and its own
buttons. Otherwise nothing changes: 2608's passing case, a recall under a
reply that asks nothing, stays inline. No new text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
